gnome-flashback: make libsystemd optional

libsystemd is used in two places: libdesktop sends the output of the
programs it starts to the journal (sd_journal_stream_fd() in
child_setup()), and libscreensaver asks sd-login for its own X11 session to
follow logind's Lock/Unlock signals.  Systems without systemd (illumos, the
BSDs) cannot build gnome-flashback at all.  Check for libsystemd once,
optionally (--with-systemd=auto|yes|no), define HAVE_SYSTEMD; without it the
started programs keep the session's stdout/stderr, and
gf_find_systemd_session() reports no session, the path the listener already
takes when it cannot determine one.  With libsystemd nothing changes.

Upstream: not yet sent (https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-flashback).

--- gnome-flashback-3.50.0/configure.ac
+++ gnome-flashback-3.50.0/configure.ac
@@ -158,7 +158,6 @@
   gio-unix-2.0 >= $GLIB_REQUIRED
   gnome-desktop-3.0 >= $LIBGNOME_DESKTOP_REQUIRED
   gtk+-3.0 >= $GTK_REQUIRED
-  libsystemd
   x11
 ])
 
@@ -230,10 +229,24 @@
   glib-2.0 >= $GLIB_REQUIRED
   gnome-desktop-3.0 >= $LIBGNOME_DESKTOP_REQUIRED
   gtk+-3.0 >= $GTK_REQUIRED
-  libsystemd
   xxf86vm >= $XXF86VM_REQUIRED
 ])
 
+dnl libsystemd is optional: the desktop sends the output of programs it
+dnl starts to the journal, and the screensaver looks up its logind session.
+dnl Without systemd the programs keep the session's stdout/stderr, and the
+dnl screensaver runs without logind (as it does when logind is absent).
+AC_ARG_WITH([systemd],
+            [AS_HELP_STRING([--without-systemd], [build without libsystemd])],
+            [with_systemd="$withval"], [with_systemd="auto"])
+AS_IF([test "x$with_systemd" != "xno"], [
+  PKG_CHECK_MODULES([SYSTEMD], [libsystemd], [have_systemd="yes"], [have_systemd="no"])
+  AS_IF([test "x$have_systemd" = "xno" && test "x$with_systemd" = "xyes"],
+        [AC_MSG_ERROR([libsystemd requested but not found])])
+], [have_systemd="no"])
+AS_IF([test "x$have_systemd" = "xyes"],
+      [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_SYSTEMD], [1], [Define if libsystemd is available])])
+
 PKG_CHECK_MODULES([SCREENSHOT], [
   gio-unix-2.0 >= $GLIB_REQUIRED
   gtk+-3.0 >= $GTK_REQUIRED
--- gnome-flashback-3.50.0/gnome-flashback/libdesktop/gf-utils.c
+++ gnome-flashback-3.50.0/gnome-flashback/libdesktop/gf-utils.c
